<p>Chambord is a fruit-based liqueur. It was created in 1982 and is made from red and black raspberries, Madagascan vanilla, Moroccan citrus peel, honey, and Cognac.</p>
<p>It’s a lovely liqueur that’s particularly good poured over ice cream.</p>
<p>And I think that’s one of the reasons some people prefer to use Chambord over Creme de Cassis: they prefer the flavour of raspberry over blackcurrant, but also it’s sweeter.</p>
